  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The reactor coolant pump is vertically installed on a cold leg of a primary
    loop of the reactor. The reactor coolant enters the suction side of the pump
    at high pressure and temperature (16 MPa, 290 \xB0C). The pump impeller accelerates
    the flow of coolant, and after that, the discharge valve converts the increased
    velocity of the coolant to pressure. At the discharge nozzle of the reactor coolant
    pump, the reactor coolant pressure will be 0.5 Mpa higher than the inlet pressure.
    After the coolant leaves the discharge side of the pump, it will enter the cold
    leg and continue to the reactor. Let us understand the working of the reactor
    coolant pump."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e63ac0177aeed334f9a24408402d8fb6, type: 2}
